{
  "description": "Services converted to the dependency-injection pattern (SWLOR.Game.Server/Readmes/DependencyInjection.md). Each is a static facade Service.<name> that forwards to the instance class <name>Service behind the interface I<name>Service, both in Domain.<domain>. SWLOR.Architecture.Tests apply their rules to exactly these services: the pieces must exist, hold no static mutable state, keep the [NWNEventHandler] methods on the facade, and not be reached for by service location. The domain must match DomainMap.json. A service made of more than one class lists the others in an optional \"extras\" array (sorted by name), each an object with either a \"facade\" (a static class of the namespace Service.<name>Service with state or event handlers, named relative to SWLOR.Game.Server.Service: it stays a static facade so handler names do not change) or a \"part\" (a class a large service is split into by responsibility, which has no facade of its own). Either way the extra has its own instance class <Type>Service behind I<Type>Service in the same domain, registered in the container, and every rule applies to it too. Add a service here, sorted by name, in the pull request that converts it. The facade of a service with parts may forward a member a part owns straight to that part's interface, and a member of the pure static class Domain.<domain>.<name>Rules straight to it (Combat), so a call goes through no other service first. There is no list of services in progress: a service is listed here only when it is fully converted. During facade removal (P2-Z) a service whose static facades the branch deleted has \"facadeRemoved\": true: it has no Service.<name> type, static code reaches it through the property of the same name on SWLOR.Game.Server.Composition.GameServices, its handlers are on its instance class, and tools/Refactor/RemovedFacades.json lists its facades. P2-ZZ removes the flag.",
